SUMMARY:Hiking 101 Workshop at Evergreen Brick Works
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Bruce Trail Club\n**New to hiking or looking to refres
 h the basics? Join the Toronto Bruce Trail Club for Hiking 101\, an approa
 chable\, interactive primer designed to get you comfortable and trail-read
 y.**\n\n**What You’ll Learn**\n![🎒](https://static.xx.fbcdn.net/image
 s/emoji.php/v9/ta4/1/16/1f392.png) **Essential Gear:** What to pack for a 
 safe\, comfortable\, and self-sufficient day on the trails.\n![❄️](htt
 ps://static.xx.fbcdn.net/images/emoji.php/v9/t2e/1/16/2744.png) **Winter H
 iking:** Practical tips and clothing layering strategies to safely extend 
 your hiking season through the winter.\n![🌱](https://static.xx.fbcdn.ne
 t/images/emoji.php/v9/t69/1/16/1f331.png) **Conservation & Biodiversity:**
  How the Toronto Bruce Trail Club works to protect and restore sensitive e
 cosystems along the Niagara Escarpment.\n![📆](https://static.xx.fbcdn.n
 et/images/emoji.php/v9/tff/1/16/1f4c6.png) **Year-Round Outings:** How to 
 join our full schedule of urban walks\, car pool hikes\, bus day trips\, a
 nd winter ski and snowshoe coach excursions.\n![❓](https://static.xx.fbc
 dn.net/images/emoji.php/v9/t4c/1/16/2753.png) **Q&A:** Dedicated time with
  experienced hike leaders to answer your questions.\n\nPlease register at:
  [https://torontobrucetrailclub.org/sign-up-for-hiking-101-at-evergreen-br
 ick-works/](https://torontobrucetrailclub.org/sign-up-for-hiking-101-at-ev
 ergreen-brick-works/)\n\nPlease email tbtchikeleaders@gmail.com if you hav
 e any questions about the workshop.\n\nThere will be two morning introduct
 ory hikes finishing in time for the Hiking 101 Workshop and we will be in 
 the Farmer's Market in the morning providing information on the Bruce Trai
 l and our hiking program.\n\nIf you would like to join us for one of two m
 orning introductory hikes before the Hiking 101 Workshop you may select on
 e at the bottom of the above registration.
